WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.972
Let's do a brand new problem from start to finish, with real numbers.

00:00:03.972 --> 00:00:09.440
An aluminum bar, fixed to a wall on the left, made of two pieces: a thick one, then a thin one.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:15.545
Then a spring connects the end of the thin piece to a second wall on the right.

00:00:15.545 --> 00:00:21.864
And a load of seven thousand newtons pushes right, at the step between the two pieces.

00:00:21.864 --> 00:00:26.420
The question: how does that load divide between the two walls?

00:00:26.753 --> 00:00:28.107
The material first.

00:00:28.107 --> 00:00:32.524
Aluminum: E is seventy thousand newtons per square millimeter.

00:00:32.524 --> 00:00:38.793
The thick piece has an area of two hundred square millimeters, the thin one one hundred.

00:00:39.153 --> 00:00:42.948
Each piece is five hundred millimeters long.

00:00:42.948 --> 00:00:49.073
And the spring's stiffness is fourteen thousand newtons per millimeter.

00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:57.662
Number the nodes: zero at the left wall, one at the step, two at the end of the thin piece, three at the right wall.

00:00:57.662 --> 00:01:02.227
We want the displacements, the stresses, and the wall reactions.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:14.493
Each piece of bar is an element, and each element is a spring with stiffness E A over l.

00:01:14.793 --> 00:01:23.609
Thick piece: seventy thousand times two hundred, over five hundred: twenty eight thousand newtons per millimeter.

00:01:23.609 --> 00:01:28.913
Thin piece: half the area, so half the stiffness, fourteen thousand.

00:01:29.246 --> 00:01:33.870
And the real spring is already a spring, fourteen thousand.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:38.886
So the whole thing is three springs in a row, between two walls.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:42.463
Four nodes, so a four by four matrix.

00:01:42.463 --> 00:01:46.292
Each of the three springs drops in its two by two block.

00:01:46.592 --> 00:01:51.952
Your turn first: pause and do checkpoint seven point one in your guide, and assemble it yourself.

00:01:55.185 --> 00:02:05.305
Element one, nodes zero and one: twenty eight thousand on the diagonal at zero and one, minus twenty eight thousand between them.

00:02:05.685 --> 00:02:09.255
Element two, nodes one and two: fourteen thousand.

00:02:09.255 --> 00:02:15.965
At spot one-one it adds to the twenty eight thousand already there, making forty two thousand.

00:02:16.352 --> 00:02:21.748
The spring, nodes two and three: fourteen thousand again.

00:02:21.748 --> 00:02:27.712
At spot two-two, fourteen plus fourteen, twenty eight thousand.

00:02:28.152 --> 00:02:40.832
The load vector: the reaction R zero at node zero, seven thousand at node one, nothing at node two, and the reaction R three at node three.

00:02:41.899 --> 00:02:46.591
Both walls are fixed, so q zero and q three are both zero.

00:02:46.591 --> 00:02:52.739
Same move as last time: cross out their columns, because they multiply zero.

00:02:53.013 --> 00:02:58.263
And set their rows aside, because those rows hold the unknown reactions.

00:02:58.263 --> 00:03:00.013
We'll come back to them.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:09.434
What's left is two by two: forty two thousand, minus fourteen thousand; minus fourteen thousand, twenty eight thousand.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:13.113
Times q one, q two, equals seven thousand, zero.

00:03:14.166 --> 00:03:15.676
Two equations.

00:03:15.676 --> 00:03:26.896
Start with the second one: minus fourteen thousand q one, plus twenty eight thousand q two, equals zero.

00:03:26.896 --> 00:03:29.486
So q one is twice q two.

00:03:29.786 --> 00:03:40.040
Put that into the first: forty two thousand times two q two, minus fourteen thousand q two, equals seven thousand.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:48.946
That's eighty four thousand minus fourteen thousand, seventy thousand q two, equals seven thousand.

00:03:49.246 --> 00:03:56.886
So q two is zero point one millimeters, and q one, twice that, is zero point two millimeters.

00:03:57.186 --> 00:03:58.057
Picture it.

00:03:58.057 --> 00:04:02.414
The step moves two tenths of a millimeter to the right.

00:04:02.414 --> 00:04:04.712
The end moves only one tenth.

00:04:04.712 --> 00:04:09.386
So the thin piece got shorter, and the spring got squeezed.

00:04:10.499 --> 00:04:18.925
Stress in each element is E times its strain: the displacement of its right node minus its left node, over its length.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.139
The same formula as the column.

00:04:21.439 --> 00:04:29.522
Thick piece: seventy thousand times zero point two minus zero, over five hundred.

00:04:29.522 --> 00:04:33.813
Twenty eight newtons per square millimeter.

00:04:33.813 --> 00:04:38.303
That unit is also called a megapascal, M P a.

00:04:38.303 --> 00:04:40.399
Positive, so tension.

00:04:40.706 --> 00:04:49.026
Your turn: pause and do checkpoint seven point two in your guide, and find the stress in the thin piece.

00:04:52.206 --> 00:05:01.547
Thin piece: seventy thousand times zero point one minus zero point two, over five hundred.

00:05:01.547 --> 00:05:05.698
Minus fourteen megapascals: compression.

00:05:05.698 --> 00:05:11.406
The load pulls the thick piece and pushes the thin one.

00:05:14.266 --> 00:05:16.596
Now the rows we set aside.

00:05:16.596 --> 00:05:25.649
Row zero: twenty eight thousand times q zero, minus twenty eight thousand times q one, equals R zero.

00:05:25.649 --> 00:05:33.626
That's minus twenty eight thousand times zero point two: minus fifty six hundred newtons.

00:05:33.926 --> 00:05:41.566
Row three: minus fourteen thousand times q two, equals R three.

00:05:41.566 --> 00:05:45.326
Minus fourteen hundred newtons.

00:05:45.626 --> 00:05:51.169
Pay close attention to this move, because problem two of your homework tests exactly this.

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:56.466
The rows we set aside to solve the system are the ones that give back the wall forces.

00:05:56.766 --> 00:05:58.724
Both reactions point left.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:04.373
At the left wall, the thick piece is in tension, so the wall pulls it back.

00:06:04.373 --> 00:06:09.646
At the right wall, the spring is squeezed, so the wall pushes it back.

00:06:09.979 --> 00:06:14.932
Together, fifty six hundred plus fourteen hundred is seven thousand.

00:06:14.932 --> 00:06:17.117
They balance the load exactly.

00:06:17.117 --> 00:06:26.659
So four fifths of the load goes to the left wall, through the stiff thick piece, and one fifth goes right, through the softer path.

00:06:26.979 --> 00:06:32.819
So, stepping back: the same recipe as the column, now with real numbers and two supports.
